163	// Owns "type information" objects created during the type checking process.
164	//
165	// In the process of type checking we may instantiate "sub type-infos" for
166	// things like particular parametric instantiations, that have
167	// parametric-independent type information as a parent (see TypeInfo::parent()).
168	//
169	// Since we decide to create these "sub type-infos" in a way that is driven by
170	// the program at type checking time, we place all type info objects into this
171	// owned pool (arena style ownership to avoid circular references or leaks or
172	// any other sort of lifetime issues).
173	class TypeInfoOwner {
174	 public:
175	  // Returns an error status iff parent is nullptr and "module" already has a
176	  // root type info.
